    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters the June 25th slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear offensive anchor, sporting an elite 77.88 score against the vulnerable 4.53 xERA of McGreevy. Despite a 42% rain risk that necessitates monitoring, **Corbin Carroll** occupies the prime #3 spot in the lineup, benefiting from a +6% boost for his high-leverage order position and an additional +6% for the platoon advantage against a right-hander. We are also leaning heavily on **Josh Naylor** (65.03) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (60.55) to drive run production; both benefit significantly from favorable lineup positioning and exploitable pitching matchups. **Jose Caballero** remains a high-upside play for our SB-starved build; while batting 8th is a drag on his score, his +13% platoon boost against Early (L) keeps him firmly in our starting mix as a potential theft threat.\n\nWe navigated a congested outfield today, with **James Wood** (51.16) ultimately securing a spot despite facing a tough left-handed arm in S\u00e1nchez (2.84 xERA). While his SP matchup carries a -19% penalty, his elite 0.401 xwOBA and lead-off status provide a floor that our bench options simply cannot match. **Max Muncy** (49.23) and **Zach McKinstry** (49.14) represent our most marginal starts, saved primarily by park factors and favorable wind conditions that offset their lower batting order assignments. Our most difficult decision was identifying the final utility spot; with **Mickey Moniak**, **Brice Turang**, and **Seiya Suzuki** all sidelined by team off-days or benchings, we lacked a true \"next man up\" to challenge the current lineup, leaving players like **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Henry Bolte** either in reserve or unavailable as we look to conserve game caps for higher-leverage future matchups.",
